### -> adaptors shipped but NOT bound in the config:
   georotationadaptor  (libhidlgeorotationadaptor-qt5.so exists)
   rotationadaptor  (libhidlrotationadaptor-qt5.so exists)
   wakeupadaptor  (libhidlwakeupadaptor-qt5.so exists)

########## 3. the data path, from the binaries themselves (strings + dynamic symbols)
### 3a. the sensor object is sensorfw's own: local.OrientationSensor lives in
###     liborientationsensor-qt5.so, and its chain is named there:
   orientationchain
   orientationsensor
   OrientationSensorChannelAdaptor
   local.OrientationSensor
   OrientationPlugin

### 3b. that chain joins the ACCELEROMETER chain plus the interpreter (liborientationchain):
   accelerometer
   PoseData
   accelerometerchain
   accelerometer/orientationinterpreter join failed

### 3c. the interpreter is a six-position classifier with explicit face handling:
   _ZN22OrientationInterpreter16rotateToPortraitEi
   _ZN22OrientationInterpreter17rotateToLandscapeEi
   _ZN22OrientationInterpreter11processFaceEv
   _ZN22OrientationInterpreter19THRESHOLD_LANDSCAPEE
   _ZN22OrientationInterpreter18THRESHOLD_PORTRAITE
   orientation/threshold_portrait
   orientation/threshold_landscape
   orientation/buffer_size

### 3d. the ONLY conversion between the accelerometer adaptor's buffer and that classifier is
###     [accelerometer] transformation_matrix, read by libaccelerometerchain-qt5.so:
   accelerometeradaptor
   accelerometer/transformation_matrix
   accelerometer/acccoordinatealigner join failed
###   and that key's live value is the IDENTITY (section 1): "1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1"

### 3e. the adaptors that are *named* orientation/rotation/georotation cannot be producing a
###     1..6 position: they all emit CompassData, i.e. degrees:
   libhidlorientationadaptor-qt5.so:  8 x CompassData,  HybrisOrientationAdaptor
   libhidlrotationadaptor-qt5.so:  8 x CompassData,  HybrisRotationAdaptor
   libhidlgeorotationadaptor-qt5.so:  8 x CompassData,  HybrisGeoRotationAdaptor

########## 4. the availability syntax is resolved through libdeviceinfo, and this port has no
##########    Feature_* keys -- so =Feature_X cannot be the reason a sensor is unavailable
$ readelf -d /mnt/zl1-rootfs/usr/sbin/sensorfwd | grep NEEDED
   libsensordatatypes-qt5.so.1
   libsensorfw-qt5.so.0
   libsystemd.so.0
   libdeviceinfo.so.0
   libQt5Core.so.5
   libstdc++.so.6
   libgcc_s.so.1
   libc.so.6
   ld-linux-aarch64.so.1
### the symbols it takes from libdeviceinfo:
   _ZN10DeviceInfo3getENSt7__cxx1112basic_stringIcSt11char_traitsIcESaIcEEES5_
   _ZN10DeviceInfoC1ENS_9PrintModeE
   _ZN10DeviceInfo8containsENSt7__cxx1112basic_stringIcSt11char_traitsIcESaIcEEE
### the literal that ties the config syntax to that library (libsensorfw-qt5.so.0.9.0):
   Feature_
   bool evaluateAvailabilityValue(const QString&, const QString&)
### and every Feature_* key in this port's deviceinfo:
   (none)

### no ssu-sysinfo anywhere in the image either:
   (none)

########## 5. every plugin in the image resolves its own dependencies (so this is not a missing
##########    library story on the UT side -- contrast with docs 90 on the Android side)
   sonames known in the image: 6233
   sensord-qt5 plugins with an unresolved dependency: 0

### and what the device's sensorfwd actually runs with (the image's unit):
   Type=notify
   ExecStart=/usr/sbin/sensorfwd --systemd --device-info --log-level=warning
   Restart=always
   RestartSec=1
